(1015511, 121955, 26526, '<td valign="top">I can see the snow on the trees, but this photograph is just too dark for me to really appreciate the snow aspect. Needs more light (white) in it. I like your composition and dof, clear city (?) lights in the background.</td>', 'I can see the snow on the trees, but this photograph is just too dark for me to really appreciate the snow aspect. Needs more light (white) in it. I like your composition and dof, clear city (?) lights in the background.', '2004-11-17 05:30:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015512, 121944, 29079, '<td valign="top">maybe the effect would have been better from a different angle....</td>', 'maybe the effect would have been better from a different angle....', '2004-11-17 05:31:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015519, 121260, 26526, '<td valign="top">I would like this photograph better if the pumpkins centered closer in the foreground, in clearer focus with more light on them. They get lost in the black background. The foreground is distracting.</td>', 'I would like this photograph better if the pumpkins centered closer in the foreground, in clearer focus with more light on them. They get lost in the black background. The foreground is distracting.', '2004-11-17 05:34:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015521, 121366, 26526, '<td valign="top">Fits the b&amp;w challenge. Creepy subject. Worms as a meal, just turns me off. Sorry.</td>', 'Fits the b&w challenge. Creepy subject. Worms as a meal, just turns me off. Sorry.', '2004-11-17 05:36:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015526, 121374, 25347, '<td valign="top">It seems a little dark in the picture.  The black and white would work well though, I love the shadows cast by the inner petals.  Also, there''s some distracting backround elements, but overall a good picture.</td>', 'It seems a little dark in the picture.  The black and white would work well though, I love the shadows cast by the inner petals.  Also, there''s some distracting backround elements, but overall a good picture.', '2004-11-17 05:41:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015527, 121527, 25347, '<td valign="top">The only thing I see a problem with is that in your blacks (the clouds) there isn''t any detail.  Also, there''s almost too much negative space for my taste, as well as what appears to be specs of dust.  It''s a good image, I love the way the rays protrude from the cloud.</td>', 'The only thing I see a problem with is that in your blacks (the clouds) there isn''t any detail.  Also, there''s almost too much negative space for my taste, as well as what appears to be specs of dust.  It''s a good image, I love the way the rays protrude from the cloud.', '2004-11-17 05:42:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015528, 120776, 25347, '<td valign="top">Maybe if the rampway was inclined?  I love the detail that black and white creates for this shot, within the trees.  The only donfall I notice is that the white is washed out on the outside of the left of the rampway, and the black hides some of the detail that could be there.  Still, a very nice capture.</td>', 'Maybe if the rampway was inclined?  I love the detail that black and white creates for this shot, within the trees.  The only donfall I notice is that the white is washed out on the outside of the left of the rampway, and the black hides some of the detail that could be there.  Still, a very nice capture.', '2004-11-17 05:43:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015529, 122058, 25347, '<td valign="top">Excellent portrait/candid.  Everything is magnificant about this except the sky seems a little washed out, so much so that it overpowers the trees and their shape and form.  I also would''ve taken the picture without the toy, but outside of that a good picture.</td>', 'Excellent portrait/candid.  Everything is magnificant about this except the sky seems a little washed out, so much so that it overpowers the trees and their shape and form.  I also would''ve taken the picture without the toy, but outside of that a good picture.', '2004-11-17 05:45:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015531, 121586, 25347, '<td valign="top">Shots like this have ribboned, and this is as good as those.  The only difference I see is that those seemed to have a more creative use of light, but outside of that, virtually identical to a ribbon winner. Good job.</td>', 'Shots like this have ribboned, and this is as good as those.  The only difference I see is that those seemed to have a more creative use of light, but outside of that, virtually identical to a ribbon winner. Good job.', '2004-11-17 05:46:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015534, 121734, 26526, '<td valign="top">Very detailed structure, in clear focus. Great in b&amp;w. I like that. I just don''t like the radical tilt of this photo. Just my opinion. I know you composed it like this on purpose for impact. Not a slightly leaning building you didn''t straighten. The longer I look at it the better I like it, will up your score.</td>', 'Very detailed structure, in clear focus. Great in b&w. I like that. I just don''t like the radical tilt of this photo. Just my opinion. I know you composed it like this on purpose for impact. Not a slightly leaning building you didn''t straighten. The longer I look at it the better I like it, will up your score.', '2004-11-17 05:47:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015535, 122155, 29079, '<td valign="top">I like the texture and lighting in here</td>', 'I like the texture and lighting in here', '2004-11-17 05:47:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015536, 121461, 25347, '<td valign="top">Aah, it''s Nam all over!  This is a good candid, but the only things I''m wary about are the border, and the swing.  The wsing overpowers the bottom of the image and (I believe) casts that hard shadow on his face.  Still, an above average picture.</td>', 'Aah, it''s Nam all over!  This is a good candid, but the only things I''m wary about are the border, and the swing.  The wsing overpowers the bottom of the image and (I believe) casts that hard shadow on his face.  Still, an above average picture.', '2004-11-17 05:48:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015538, 120606, 25347, '<td valign="top">Very good artistic use of lighting, excellent take on the challenge.  I expect this one to score highly (as well as have 50 1''s, 2''s or 3''s).  The only thing I think to make this picture better would be to have her turn her hand so her fingers aren''t illuminated.  But still, a superb photo.</td>', 'Very good artistic use of lighting, excellent take on the challenge.  I expect this one to score highly (as well as have 50 1''s, 2''s or 3''s).  The only thing I think to make this picture better would be to have her turn her hand so her fingers aren''t illuminated.  But still, a superb photo.', '2004-11-17 05:49:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015539, 122005, 26526, '<td valign="top">Surfacing from what? I can''t figure this photograph out. I like the lines in it.</td>', 'Surfacing from what? I can''t figure this photograph out. I like the lines in it.', '2004-11-17 05:50:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015541, 120407, 26526, '<td valign="top">This photograph is too dark, not enough detail in it, for me to figure it out. Sorry.</td>', 'This photograph is too dark, not enough detail in it, for me to figure it out. Sorry.', '2004-11-17 05:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015543, 121811, 25347, '<td valign="top">I would''ve just used the word stubborn, because as I''ve discovered, voters aren''t the most knowledgable people ;).  This is a good pose, and I think the background works well, but I think the subject should be looking up at the camera.  If he were to look up at the camera, and make a stubborn face, It would assuredly exude recalcitrance :D.</td>', 'I would''ve just used the word stubborn, because as I''ve discovered, voters aren''t the most knowledgable people ;).  This is a good pose, and I think the background works well, but I think the subject should be looking up at the camera.  If he were to look up at the camera, and make a stubborn face, It would assuredly exude recalcitrance :D.', '2004-11-17 05:53:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015544, 121458, 25347, '<td valign="top">An interesting composition.  I just think that the palm tree, and the tree behind it, are too dark.  Also, the figures don''t seem to possess much much definition, there''s not much contrast between the figures and the tres.  It''s almost like two seperate objects, and my eyes seem to switch between the two, unsure of which to look at.  Still, the composition is a good idea, definitely photo worthy.</td>', 'An interesting composition.  I just think that the palm tree, and the tree behind it, are too dark.  Also, the figures don''t seem to possess much much definition, there''s not much contrast between the figures and the tres.  It''s almost like two seperate objects, and my eyes seem to switch between the two, unsure of which to look at.  Still, the composition is a good idea, definitely photo worthy.', '2004-11-17 05:56:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015547, 121269, 25347, '<td valign="top">Beautiful model, however without the title it loses the humor and just becomes a model shot.  In which case, the average voter is going to vote down, because it''s a model shot.  But that aside, it''s an excellent picture technically, There''s no indecision in what subject I should look at  ;o).  I wouldn''t have gone with the title though, I''m sure you''ll get knocked around for it.  It probably would''ve scored higher otherwise.</td>', 'Beautiful model, however without the title it loses the humor and just becomes a model shot.  In which case, the average voter is going to vote down, because it''s a model shot.  But that aside, it''s an excellent picture technically, There''s no indecision in what subject I should look at  ;o).  I wouldn''t have gone with the title though, I''m sure you''ll get knocked around for it.  It probably would''ve scored higher otherwise.', '2004-11-17 05:58:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1015548, 121399, 25347, '<td valign="top">First thought:  woah... *blink*<br/> <br/>Interesting idea.  Would''ve been good for the parallel lines challenge.  I like the way you can see not just hte ones in the foreground, but also distinguish the ones farther away.  This probably isn''t under your control, but it just seems that in the whites on the tree trunks, it''s washed out and you lose some detail.  Outside of that though, stunning (and dizzying) picture.</td>', 'First thought:  woah... *blink* Interesting idea.  Would''ve been good for the parallel lines challenge.  I like the way you can see not just hte ones in the foreground, but also distinguish the ones farther away.  This probably isn''t under your control, but it just seems that in the whites on the tree trunks, it''s washed out and you lose some detail.  Outside of that though, stunning (and dizzying) picture.', '2004-11-17 06:00:43.000000', NULL, 1),
