(1016282, 120819, 6388, '<td valign="top">to me, pgotography is primarily about light.  this one could either use a little more or a little less, depending on what you''re going for.  I really like the backlighting idea using the firbeglass wall (a shed or barn I''d assume), but the cannisters seem like they need to either be brought out a bit, or completely silhouetted. A single spot light cast from the direction of your camera would help i think.   if this weren''t a basic challenge, you could dodge the cannisters a bit and just bring out the highlights a wee bit.  This is just my opinnion of course - ignore it if this is the look you''re going for :) 6 from me.<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'to me, pgotography is primarily about light.  this one could either use a little more or a little less, depending on what you''re going for.  I really like the backlighting idea using the firbeglass wall (a shed or barn I''d assume), but the cannisters seem like they need to either be brought out a bit, or completely silhouetted. A single spot light cast from the direction of your camera would help i think.   if this weren''t a basic challenge, you could dodge the cannisters a bit and just bring out the highlights a wee bit.  This is just my opinnion of course - ignore it if this is the look you''re going for :) 6 from me. P', '2004-11-17 11:21:03.000000', NULL, 1),
