(1016510, 120995, 29576, '<td valign="top">Great picture! Its a very freaky tree. I am not skilled in this art, but I know what I like.  The only but I find is that the picture is a bit off center.</td>', 'Great picture! Its a very freaky tree. I am not skilled in this art, but I know what I like.  The only but I find is that the picture is a bit off center.', '2004-11-17 12:14:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016511, 122148, 3087, '<td valign="top">What an interesting image - certainly the kind of idea I could see used in stock photography and taken on by some firm in some clever and slick advertising campaign.<br/>Main downsides for me:<br/>1) Composition - the panoramic really doesn''t work for me - I like the white space to the left of the pretzels but would prefer to see more of that lower one. Perhaps another third of the height that exists added to the bottom of the frame?<br/>2) With the exception of the background there are no real whites and very few blacks. The tonal range seems very low. That makes it feel a little bland. Boosting contrast helps a little on that front.<br/>I will email you a rough idea of what I mean with composition.<br/>Kavey</td>', 'What an interesting image - certainly the kind of idea I could see used in stock photography and taken on by some firm in some clever and slick advertising campaign.Main downsides for me:1) Composition - the panoramic really doesn''t work for me - I like the white space to the left of the pretzels but would prefer to see more of that lower one. Perhaps another third of the height that exists added to the bottom of the frame?2) With the exception of the background there are no real whites and very few blacks. The tonal range seems very low. That makes it feel a little bland. Boosting contrast helps a little on that front.I will email you a rough idea of what I mean with composition.Kavey', '2004-11-17 12:14:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016512, 122027, 29511, '<td valign="top">OOOOOOOh, i like this one.. it grips me! and i love the tattered chair amongst the haggered old trees and the bending path.. great framing and light, would have enjoyed a crisper look on the twigs and what not though</td>', 'OOOOOOOh, i like this one.. it grips me! and i love the tattered chair amongst the haggered old trees and the bending path.. great framing and light, would have enjoyed a crisper look on the twigs and what not though', '2004-11-17 12:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016517, 121588, 29535, '<td valign="top">Why did he fail?  Great pic.</td>', 'Why did he fail?  Great pic.', '2004-11-17 12:15:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016518, 120457, 29511, '<td valign="top">love the textures and feeling of this one lights perfect too... dont know if we need the top of the shed (above the pumps) but none the less bravo bravo!</td>', 'love the textures and feeling of this one lights perfect too... dont know if we need the top of the shed (above the pumps) but none the less bravo bravo!', '2004-11-17 12:15:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016519, 121623, 29511, '<td valign="top">not bad, a bit faded, and focus is blurry on the shote.. but i like the balance</td>', 'not bad, a bit faded, and focus is blurry on the shote.. but i like the balance', '2004-11-17 12:16:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016521, 120551, 6388, '<td valign="top">hm.  i commented on this already and it disappeared.  I''ll try again.<br/> <br/>i look at this and think: "there''s a picture of a sculpture".  I''d like to see some of your own creative vision thrown into it.  What do you like about it?  is it the texture or the lines or the shadows?  For me the surroundings look like they might make som nice contrasting lines, but the crop virtually eliminates them from the composition.  When i take a photo i figure my job is to make the viewer see things *my* way.  It''s what differentiates the artist from the historian.  just my opinion of course - if you don''t share it, you''re welcome to ignore me :)<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'hm.  i commented on this already and it disappeared.  I''ll try again. i look at this and think: "there''s a picture of a sculpture".  I''d like to see some of your own creative vision thrown into it.  What do you like about it?  is it the texture or the lines or the shadows?  For me the surroundings look like they might make som nice contrasting lines, but the crop virtually eliminates them from the composition.  When i take a photo i figure my job is to make the viewer see things *my* way.  It''s what differentiates the artist from the historian.  just my opinion of course - if you don''t share it, you''re welcome to ignore me :) P', '2004-11-17 12:16:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016524, 120558, 4536, '<td valign="top">This is awesome, love the way the light hits the cloumns. An added bonus would have been someone''s shadow cast in the formost beam.....</td>', 'This is awesome, love the way the light hits the cloumns. An added bonus would have been someone''s shadow cast in the formost beam.....', '2004-11-17 12:16:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016525, 122035, 29535, '<td valign="top">Perfect composition and exposure, well done.</td>', 'Perfect composition and exposure, well done.', '2004-11-17 12:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016526, 121009, 29511, '<td valign="top">like the shape of this one but the lamp post shadow and the twigs running over the man make it a bit confusin, but i really do enjoy the angle and textures used</td>', 'like the shape of this one but the lamp post shadow and the twigs running over the man make it a bit confusin, but i really do enjoy the angle and textures used', '2004-11-17 12:17:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016527, 121634, 3087, '<td valign="top">A great pose nicely positioned within the frame to provide a strong composition. <br/>Main problem for me on this one is not the slightly shallow depth of field but the plane of focus - which bits you''ve chosen to focus on. The nearside whiskers and the mouth are out of focus and yet are part of the more interesting elements of the image. I like the range of dark and light backgrounds - the light bit emphasises the shape of the cat, the dark bit shows off the whiskers that are more in focus. That said overall it feels quite dark.</td>', 'A great pose nicely positioned within the frame to provide a strong composition. Main problem for me on this one is not the slightly shallow depth of field but the plane of focus - which bits you''ve chosen to focus on. The nearside whiskers and the mouth are out of focus and yet are part of the more interesting elements of the image. I like the range of dark and light backgrounds - the light bit emphasises the shape of the cat, the dark bit shows off the whiskers that are more in focus. That said overall it feels quite dark.', '2004-11-17 12:17:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1016528, 120486, 29535, '<td valign="top">Wow. NICE!  Very nice.</td>', 'Wow. NICE!  Very nice.', '2004-11-17 12:17:41.000000', NULL, 1),
