(1018760, 121346, 9668, '<td valign="top">This shot looks horrible, the color are way off! I don''t know what you were thinking?<br/> <br/>My only critique would be that the top of the lilly seems a tad bright, but you''ve done an excellent job with this tough subject. Lighting is the key, and you''ve nailed it.</td>', 'This shot looks horrible, the color are way off! I don''t know what you were thinking? My only critique would be that the top of the lilly seems a tad bright, but you''ve done an excellent job with this tough subject. Lighting is the key, and you''ve nailed it.', '2004-11-17 23:26:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018762, 120415, 24138, '<td valign="top">black and white</td>', 'black and white', '2004-11-17 23:27:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018764, 122058, 9668, '<td valign="top">I like this expression. Nice off screen expectation, good lighting. But the shot doesn''t stand out to me for some reason.</td>', 'I like this expression. Nice off screen expectation, good lighting. But the shot doesn''t stand out to me for some reason.', '2004-11-17 23:28:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018766, 121348, 23577, '<td valign="top">Nice Lighting</td>', 'Nice Lighting', '2004-11-17 23:29:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018767, 121980, 9668, '<td valign="top">Cool composition, fits the rule of thirds pretty well. Nice tones - gray to dark gray, to stark black and white, to white.</td>', 'Cool composition, fits the rule of thirds pretty well. Nice tones - gray to dark gray, to stark black and white, to white.', '2004-11-17 23:29:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018768, 120744, 23577, '<td valign="top">eeri!</td>', 'eeri!', '2004-11-17 23:29:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018770, 120450, 9668, '<td valign="top">Seems a bit oversharpened. Don''t really get title (refering a movie called "roots?"). But I do like the shot. Nature is amazing, and you''ve captured one example.</td>', 'Seems a bit oversharpened. Don''t really get title (refering a movie called "roots?"). But I do like the shot. Nature is amazing, and you''ve captured one example.', '2004-11-17 23:30:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018771, 121640, 23577, '<td valign="top">I really like the lighting in this photo!</td>', 'I really like the lighting in this photo!', '2004-11-17 23:31:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018774, 121918, 23577, '<td valign="top">Would have given this photo a higher mark if you would have framed it with the fence more!</td>', 'Would have given this photo a higher mark if you would have framed it with the fence more!', '2004-11-17 23:33:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018777, 121932, 22384, '<td valign="top">This photo has the possibility to be breathtaking. I think the high contrast intensity of the lights distracts from what otherwise is a brilliant photo. Tone those done and let the amazing composition and your eye for a great picture take over and speak for themselves. Wow! what a great idea for a piece.</td>', 'This photo has the possibility to be breathtaking. I think the high contrast intensity of the lights distracts from what otherwise is a brilliant photo. Tone those done and let the amazing composition and your eye for a great picture take over and speak for themselves. Wow! what a great idea for a piece.', '2004-11-17 23:36:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018779, 121610, 16148, '<td valign="top">This is a nice portrait but I feel there is a little to much empty space above your subjects heads.</td>', 'This is a nice portrait but I feel there is a little to much empty space above your subjects heads.', '2004-11-17 23:38:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018781, 122115, 22384, '<td valign="top">How can you go wrong with unfurling fronds? Crop it closer and let it take over the picture. Nice detail in the foreground. The background is too much and too soft to complement your focal point, which is stunning by the way.</td>', 'How can you go wrong with unfurling fronds? Crop it closer and let it take over the picture. Nice detail in the foreground. The background is too much and too soft to complement your focal point, which is stunning by the way.', '2004-11-17 23:39:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018783, 122148, 22384, '<td valign="top">Fun idea, but the values are too limited and huge while space just doesn''t work well for me. The cropping of the bottom pretzel is too symetrical; cutting image right in the midline makes it seem contrived rather than random.</td>', 'Fun idea, but the values are too limited and huge while space just doesn''t work well for me. The cropping of the bottom pretzel is too symetrical; cutting image right in the midline makes it seem contrived rather than random.', '2004-11-17 23:41:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018785, 121453, 23913, '<td valign="top">nice shot i lov the comp. and the sky in this shot</td>', 'nice shot i lov the comp. and the sky in this shot', '2004-11-17 23:42:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018792, 120995, 16148, '<td valign="top">This image has a lot of potential.  You have found an interesting subject.  I would like to see the tree a less centered.  A little more space to the right and above would make it more appealing.  Your image is also small and this might hurt your score.</td>', 'This image has a lot of potential.  You have found an interesting subject.  I would like to see the tree a less centered.  A little more space to the right and above would make it more appealing.  Your image is also small and this might hurt your score.', '2004-11-17 23:48:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018796, 121958, 23913, '<td valign="top">nice stang the only thing that bothers me is the clutter in the upper right of the pic.<br/> <br/>GL and nice car</td>', 'nice stang the only thing that bothers me is the clutter in the upper right of the pic. GL and nice car', '2004-11-17 23:56:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018799, 121159, 23913, '<td valign="top">wonderful image like the grayscale</td>', 'wonderful image like the grayscale', '2004-11-17 23:58:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018804, 121773, 23913, '<td valign="top">it doesn''t look as dark as it should for it to be a real storm comming but i like the shot so GL</td>', 'it doesn''t look as dark as it should for it to be a real storm comming but i like the shot so GL', '2004-11-18 00:01:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018806, 121639, 4805, '<td valign="top">One of my favourites in the challenge. Perfect exposure, and DOF is nice to leave the texture in the trees behind without being too intruding on the subject. When I first saw it I thought it would benefit from lifting the camera''s perspective so that her head doesn''t cut into the trees behind, but it''s fine as it is. Good luck...</td>', 'One of my favourites in the challenge. Perfect exposure, and DOF is nice to leave the texture in the trees behind without being too intruding on the subject. When I first saw it I thought it would benefit from lifting the camera''s perspective so that her head doesn''t cut into the trees behind, but it''s fine as it is. Good luck...', '2004-11-18 00:02:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018807, 120539, 25464, '<td valign="top">A ribbon in my opinion. 10.</td>', 'A ribbon in my opinion. 10.', '2004-11-18 00:05:17.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1018808, 122172, 25028, '<td valign="top">minunat!  very interesting interplay of light and shade, positive and negative space, bright and dark surfaces.  i find the dialogue between the tangible and the intangible (actual object and its projection) particularly interesting.  also, the way in which the light circulates in the image and the multiple channels through which it reaches the viewer  makes for a subtle story--light, and not the chandelier, becomes the protagonist of your photograph.  the more i look at this image, the cooler i find it :)  it challenges the distinction between material and immaterial space, real and imagined world.  the chandelier--the tangible object--leads me to the space of shadows and projections, a space in which i can redefine reality...  and then, which of the two dimensions is real?  and what is reality?  VERY cool...</td>', 'minunat!  very interesting interplay of light and shade, positive and negative space, bright and dark surfaces.  i find the dialogue between the tangible and the intangible (actual object and its projection) particularly interesting.  also, the way in which the light circulates in the image and the multiple channels through which it reaches the viewer  makes for a subtle story--light, and not the chandelier, becomes the protagonist of your photograph.  the more i look at this image, the cooler i find it :)  it challenges the distinction between material and immaterial space, real and imagined world.  the chandelier--the tangible object--leads me to the space of shadows and projections, a space in which i can redefine reality...  and then, which of the two dimensions is real?  and what is reality?  VERY cool...', '2004-11-18 00:06:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018809, 120606, 19260, '<td valign="top">good contrast, i like the composition.</td>', 'good contrast, i like the composition.', '2004-11-18 00:07:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018812, 121640, 3214, '<td valign="top">I love the lighting and tones in this one.  A winner.</td>', 'I love the lighting and tones in this one.  A winner.', '2004-11-18 00:09:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018813, 121529, 25464, '<td valign="top">This is definitely going to win some major cutie pie points.  Tones are wonderful.  The childs face appears a little overexposed, but judging from the coloring of daddy''s face I would say it is probably due to beautiful, light skin tones rather than lighting problems.  Maybe a little too much nostil in this pose; however, the mood and the expressions more than compensate for any minor distractions.  I am guessing top 10.  Scoring a 9 from me.</td>', 'This is definitely going to win some major cutie pie points.  Tones are wonderful.  The childs face appears a little overexposed, but judging from the coloring of daddy''s face I would say it is probably due to beautiful, light skin tones rather than lighting problems.  Maybe a little too much nostil in this pose; however, the mood and the expressions more than compensate for any minor distractions.  I am guessing top 10.  Scoring a 9 from me.', '2004-11-18 00:11:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018816, 120812, 25464, '<td valign="top">I really like this one.  The lighting is dramatic and is used very effectively to highlight the best features.  GREAT eyes.  Her face is a bit angular, so the use of the chair and the angles created by the positioning of the arms works wonderfully to offset and enhance her look.  9.</td>', 'I really like this one.  The lighting is dramatic and is used very effectively to highlight the best features.  GREAT eyes.  Her face is a bit angular, so the use of the chair and the angles created by the positioning of the arms works wonderfully to offset and enhance her look.  9.', '2004-11-18 00:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018821, 120606, 23913, '<td valign="top">i like the focus as well as the grascale of this shot,and the subject isn''t so bad eigther-lol<br/> <br/>GL and well done</td>', 'i like the focus as well as the grascale of this shot,and the subject isn''t so bad eigther-lol GL and well done', '2004-11-18 00:18:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018822, 121610, 12253, '<td valign="top">Nice tones, pose and clarity with the boys.  I like negative space in it''s place but I don''t really see the use here.  I suggest eventually cropping a lot of the top.</td>', 'Nice tones, pose and clarity with the boys.  I like negative space in it''s place but I don''t really see the use here.  I suggest eventually cropping a lot of the top.', '2004-11-18 00:19:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018826, 121481, 12253, '<td valign="top">I like the dark tones and the negative space at the bottom.  I am less sure of the crop you chose at the right.  Personally, I think the head would have been good here, or at least the neck.  More significantly however, the subject has lines from their clothes that are distracting to the tones and texture of the skin.  Your model needs to avoid tight fitting underwear the day of the shoot.</td>', 'I like the dark tones and the negative space at the bottom.  I am less sure of the crop you chose at the right.  Personally, I think the head would have been good here, or at least the neck.  More significantly however, the subject has lines from their clothes that are distracting to the tones and texture of the skin.  Your model needs to avoid tight fitting underwear the day of the shoot.', '2004-11-18 00:22:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018829, 121940, 28337, '<td valign="top">too much blank sky</td>', 'too much blank sky', '2004-11-18 00:24:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018830, 122023, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very nice!   In an editing challenge, I would have liked to see the rail erased, but fine here.  Good tones.<br/> <br/>...Another alien caught on camera (see my portfolio and you''ll see what I mean!)...</td>', 'Very nice!   In an editing challenge, I would have liked to see the rail erased, but fine here.  Good tones. ...Another alien caught on camera (see my portfolio and you''ll see what I mean!)...', '2004-11-18 00:24:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018832, 122012, 15511, '<td valign="top">i wish it was bigger, it looks interesting.</td>', 'i wish it was bigger, it looks interesting.', '2004-11-18 00:25:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018837, 120558, 12253, '<td valign="top">Super!  I really like this.  However, I think it would be even better with a crop at the top.  That would put the diminishing part (via perspective) of the round part of the base into the diagonal of the shot (mostly).  I am suggesting about cutting more than 1/2 of the vertical striped area of the columns in the crop: try it and perhaps you''ll see what I mean.</td>', 'Super!  I really like this.  However, I think it would be even better with a crop at the top.  That would put the diminishing part (via perspective) of the round part of the base into the diagonal of the shot (mostly).  I am suggesting about cutting more than 1/2 of the vertical striped area of the columns in the crop: try it and perhaps you''ll see what I mean.', '2004-11-18 00:30:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1018845, 122166, 15511, '<td valign="top">About a third of ''em!</td>', 'About a third of ''em!', '2004-11-18 00:34:38.000000', NULL, 1),
