(1030603, 122021, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by xian:</b></div><hr/><i> would have been a better choice for a color challenge </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I agree ... here''s the color version of the same shot for comparison.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=123563" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/1031/thumb/123563.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/1031/thumb/123563.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/1031/thumb/123563.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>However, I still think it was probably my best picture during the challenge time period.<br/> <br/>It was also somewhat a deliberate choice to present the voters with something so obviously "better" presented in color in B+W ... forcing a few, as they said, to do a "double-take" and check to see that there really is a lot of shading and detail there ... It is also intended to be documentary in nature -- the mural is not my work after all, and that''s a challenge in itself -- to take a colorful scene and render it in grays because you have to -- instead of just looking for something which looks good in gray to start with.</td>', 'Originally posted by xian: would have been a better choice for a color challenge  I agree ... here''s the color version of the same shot for comparison.   However, I still think it was probably my best picture during the challenge time period. It was also somewhat a deliberate choice to present the voters with something so obviously "better" presented in color in B+W ... forcing a few, as they said, to do a "double-take" and check to see that there really is a lot of shading and detail there ... It is also intended to be documentary in nature -- the mural is not my work after all, and that''s a challenge in itself -- to take a colorful scene and render it in grays because you have to -- instead of just looking for something which looks good in gray to start with.', '2004-11-24 02:46:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030608, 122021, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Shadowrain:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice capture.  A different angle would have made this so much better. Maybe from the side so you could also see some of the artist''s expression as well as the mural. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I was deliberately trying to shoot from angles such that the person''s face would not be individually identifiable to allow for greater freedom in use of the photo without needing a release.</td>', 'Originally posted by Shadowrain: Nice capture.  A different angle would have made this so much better. Maybe from the side so you could also see some of the artist''s expression as well as the mural.  I was deliberately trying to shoot from angles such that the person''s face would not be individually identifiable to allow for greater freedom in use of the photo without needing a release.', '2004-11-24 02:48:44.000000', NULL, 0),
