(1030648, 120725, 27440, '<td valign="top">Oh my my my :)<br/> <br/>There is nothing better then a creative shot. I prefer the ones that are strait out of the box :) This is one of them.<br/> <br/>I am realy realy suprised this shot came out 186! Come on people can''t you apreciate novelty and creativity? I wonder who gave this shot a 1!!! Maybe he could justify his judgement? <br/> <br/>Any way congrats on this incredible shot and creativity!</td>', 'Oh my my my :) There is nothing better then a creative shot. I prefer the ones that are strait out of the box :) This is one of them. I am realy realy suprised this shot came out 186! Come on people can''t you apreciate novelty and creativity? I wonder who gave this shot a 1!!! Maybe he could justify his judgement?  Any way congrats on this incredible shot and creativity!', '2004-11-24 03:25:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030652, 122188, 27440, '<td valign="top">Congratulations. This place is amazing. It somehow makes me feel almost the same as in the film Hypercube, but without blades :)</td>', 'Congratulations. This place is amazing. It somehow makes me feel almost the same as in the film Hypercube, but without blades :)', '2004-11-24 03:28:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030656, 121183, 27440, '<td valign="top">Yes, well ... ... ... ASTONISHING.<br/> <br/>You know if I were you I would have moved the sun to the right a bit :P Hahaha just joking - flawless.</td>', 'Yes, well ... ... ... ASTONISHING. You know if I were you I would have moved the sun to the right a bit :P Hahaha just joking - flawless.', '2004-11-24 03:30:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030658, 120429, 13523, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the comments...<br/> <br/>"There are a couple annoying smudge and a weird glare on the bottom left"<br/> <br/>There is some dust in my camera, and as the use of the clone brush in ps is not allowed the dust can be seen in the picture...<br/> <br/>"I don''t care much for that little piece of thumb in the lower left. I would have liked either more, or none at all, better."<br/> <br/>I agree, the thumb in the left corner should have been positioned higher and more to the left...<br/> <br/>Regards<br/> <br/>Guðni<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-24 06:15:05.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for the comments... "There are a couple annoying smudge and a weird glare on the bottom left" There is some dust in my camera, and as the use of the clone brush in ps is not allowed the dust can be seen in the picture... "I don''t care much for that little piece of thumb in the lower left. I would have liked either more, or none at all, better." I agree, the thumb in the left corner should have been positioned higher and more to the left... Regards Guðni', '2004-11-24 03:32:12.000000', '2004-11-24 06:15:05.000000', 0),
(1030660, 121671, 27440, '<td valign="top">And another very creative shot! When I saw this one I was amazed and stoned to the chair. I see this picture on the 1 , 2, 3, 4 place! Not lower! People who gave a 1 or 2 or 3 to this pic should be banned for voting :)<br/> <br/>I bet you''re happy with the result... well don''t be <b>YOU''ve BEEN ROBBED</b>!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-24 03:34:01.</i></td>', 'And another very creative shot! When I saw this one I was amazed and stoned to the chair. I see this picture on the 1 , 2, 3, 4 place! Not lower! People who gave a 1 or 2 or 3 to this pic should be banned for voting :) I bet you''re happy with the result... well don''t be YOU''ve BEEN ROBBED!', '2004-11-24 03:33:28.000000', '2004-11-24 03:34:01.000000', 0),
(1030668, 121131, 6804, '<td valign="top">I am glad to see this one still did very well. It is just an awesome capture!</td>', 'I am glad to see this one still did very well. It is just an awesome capture!', '2004-11-24 03:40:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030676, 121482, 29462, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments well pleased with first challenge entry, yeah the top and bottom crop is as the shot I just got to tight on it lessoned learned, Thanks again</td>', 'Thanks for the comments well pleased with first challenge entry, yeah the top and bottom crop is as the shot I just got to tight on it lessoned learned, Thanks again', '2004-11-24 03:55:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030681, 121238, 11800, '<td valign="top">I guess that''s me that said it should be off center. Have it centered. What I was thinking of was the parts that show the earth thru them. To get rid of those, you would need to crop. They tend to bring more reality to the picture than is warranted.<br/>Sorry I didn''t pick up on your visualization of the picture. I did give you a six.</td>', 'I guess that''s me that said it should be off center. Have it centered. What I was thinking of was the parts that show the earth thru them. To get rid of those, you would need to crop. They tend to bring more reality to the picture than is warranted.Sorry I didn''t pick up on your visualization of the picture. I did give you a six.', '2004-11-24 04:02:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030687, 121108, 6576, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your great comments and your votes.  I was trying all that week to get a good b/w photo, but couldn''t get what I wanted.  When I when grocery shopping I saw these flowers.  The flowers were red and yellow stripes.  I put it in the front of the window with the sun shine in.  After probably 50 shots, I got the one above.</td>', 'Thanks for your great comments and your votes.  I was trying all that week to get a good b/w photo, but couldn''t get what I wanted.  When I when grocery shopping I saw these flowers.  The flowers were red and yellow stripes.  I put it in the front of the window with the sun shine in.  After probably 50 shots, I got the one above.', '2004-11-24 04:37:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030689, 121459, 24969, '<td valign="top">Make that 4 favs. Who in their right mind would give this a 1 or a 2? (Sometimes I just don''t get this place.)<br/> <br/>Very nice shot. Hope I get to visit there someday. :-)</td>', 'Make that 4 favs. Who in their right mind would give this a 1 or a 2? (Sometimes I just don''t get this place.) Very nice shot. Hope I get to visit there someday. :-)', '2004-11-24 04:39:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030697, 120762, 2780, '<td valign="top">I have this a 7, I thought it was really nice.</td>', 'I have this a 7, I thought it was really nice.', '2004-11-24 04:47:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030698, 121655, 17850, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments. My choice was not to let more light in, so the viewer''s eye to "ask for more inside the darkness".<br/>I tried more than 50 times to get this final shot. I used the b/w mode of my Nikon and there was not much processing except from a "brave" croping.<br/>As many people didn''t like darkness here, the photo finally was not competitive. But this is my first entry to DPC so I hope to be improved in future challenges.<br/></td>', 'Thanks for your comments. My choice was not to let more light in, so the viewer''s eye to "ask for more inside the darkness".I tried more than 50 times to get this final shot. I used the b/w mode of my Nikon and there was not much processing except from a "brave" croping.As many people didn''t like darkness here, the photo finally was not competitive. But this is my first entry to DPC so I hope to be improved in future challenges.', '2004-11-24 04:47:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030702, 120647, 29168, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kdolso:</b></div><hr/><i> I absolutely love this image. The hopefulness of having the flower face to the right, the water drops which symbolized the tears of healing for me. The values in the flower and the crispness of the petals are superb. ...</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you kdolso for being the only commenter to take the title and see beyond "Yet another pretty flower close-up but with an ugly fence." The setting is exactly as I found it. "Zero interference" is my policy, for now.<br/> <br/>Thanks to everyone else who took the time to comment. With 683 entries it must have been tempting to leave comments out altogether! I''m certainly gaining an idea of what poeple like and what they don''t. Great stuff! Thanks again.<br/> <br/>Someone commented on the rose''s focus being a little off. It is? Or was it(CRT) monitor glare? The focus is very near perfect on my screen. &lt;shrug&gt; Hmmm, I guess the furtherest two petals are a little out of focus around the very edges. Pity I don''t have the luxry of an SLR camera to see these things when the button goes down. One day... &lt;sigh&gt;</td>', 'Originally posted by kdolso: I absolutely love this image. The hopefulness of having the flower face to the right, the water drops which symbolized the tears of healing for me. The values in the flower and the crispness of the petals are superb. ...  Thank you kdolso for being the only commenter to take the title and see beyond "Yet another pretty flower close-up but with an ugly fence." The setting is exactly as I found it. "Zero interference" is my policy, for now. Thanks to everyone else who took the time to comment. With 683 entries it must have been tempting to leave comments out altogether! I''m certainly gaining an idea of what poeple like and what they don''t. Great stuff! Thanks again. Someone commented on the rose''s focus being a little off. It is? Or was it(CRT) monitor glare? The focus is very near perfect on my screen. <shrug> Hmmm, I guess the furtherest two petals are a little out of focus around the very edges. Pity I don''t have the luxry of an SLR camera to see these things when the button goes down. One day... <sigh>', '2004-11-24 04:49:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030705, 121699, 5746, '<td valign="top">Hmm, I think it deserves to be in top 20. Never mind. You have great potential. This is your best entry IMHO. In this hectic challenge you are in top 100. Congratulations :)</td>', 'Hmm, I think it deserves to be in top 20. Never mind. You have great potential. This is your best entry IMHO. In this hectic challenge you are in top 100. Congratulations :)', '2004-11-24 04:52:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1030714, 121812, 29196, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Gatorguy:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a very nice photograph.  I will say, however, that I find the title a little insulting to my intelligence.  Don''t you think the average viewer will "get it?".  Maybe this is your sense of humor... maybe I just don''t understand.   In any event, based solely on the merits of the photograph, I give this one an 8 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I had absolutely no purpose to insult nobody. I was just kidding with the challenge subject. Thanks for your comment about the photograph.</td>', 'Originally posted by Gatorguy: This is a very nice photograph.  I will say, however, that I find the title a little insulting to my intelligence.  Don''t you think the average viewer will "get it?".  Maybe this is your sense of humor... maybe I just don''t understand.   In any event, based solely on the merits of the photograph, I give this one an 8   I had absolutely no purpose to insult nobody. I was just kidding with the challenge subject. Thanks for your comment about the photograph.', '2004-11-24 04:59:36.000000', NULL, 0),
