(1031799, 122053, 2741, '<td valign="top">"This was actually a self portrait, i had 10 sec. to run up the hill "pose", go back, and repeated it several times, until i was happy with it"<br/> <br/>Thats alot of effort.<br/> <br/>Several Times... meaning at least 7 times....  You must of been out of breath, and I bet you are in much better running shape, then you were before the challenge. :)<br/> <br/>Great shot.  <br/> <br/>I am out of breath now.</td>', '"This was actually a self portrait, i had 10 sec. to run up the hill "pose", go back, and repeated it several times, until i was happy with it" Thats alot of effort. Several Times... meaning at least 7 times....  You must of been out of breath, and I bet you are in much better running shape, then you were before the challenge. :) Great shot.   I am out of breath now.', '2004-11-24 17:05:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1031817, 120613, 29332, '<td valign="top">The photo is really focussed but because I had to shrink it for the rules of contest, it lost its quality. I KNOW HOW TO FOCUS A CAMERA!</td>', 'The photo is really focussed but because I had to shrink it for the rules of contest, it lost its quality. I KNOW HOW TO FOCUS A CAMERA!', '2004-11-24 17:18:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1031846, 121529, 20662, '<td valign="top">Artyste and dipaulk<br/> <br/>Thank you for your comments. I wanted to let you know that is was the palest child I have ever photographed, the lights positively glowed off her translucent skin. Compared to how dark her father''s skin was I having a terrible time getting her to look natural. Had this been a members challenge I could have spot edited giving her a little more depth and more color. In the end I decided to go with this shot because I love the look on her dad''s face. Everyone should have dad look that happy when hugged by his little girl. I''m in no way complaining about how this photo placed -- 121 is really good in a challenge os 638 very well done photos -- Debi</td>', 'Artyste and dipaulk Thank you for your comments. I wanted to let you know that is was the palest child I have ever photographed, the lights positively glowed off her translucent skin. Compared to how dark her father''s skin was I having a terrible time getting her to look natural. Had this been a members challenge I could have spot edited giving her a little more depth and more color. In the end I decided to go with this shot because I love the look on her dad''s face. Everyone should have dad look that happy when hugged by his little girl. I''m in no way complaining about how this photo placed -- 121 is really good in a challenge os 638 very well done photos -- Debi', '2004-11-24 17:33:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1031848, 120762, 25150, '<td valign="top">I just left a comment in the forums on this image. I''ll repeat it here:<br/> <br/>"I see a uniqueness in this image. I also see a wonderful example of simplicity. There is not much to look at, It''s easy on the eyes, and mind. I also did not vote on this challenge, but i would have rated it very high."<br/> <br/>I think this is a wonderful image, and i''m really disapointed it was rated so low.</td>', 'I just left a comment in the forums on this image. I''ll repeat it here: "I see a uniqueness in this image. I also see a wonderful example of simplicity. There is not much to look at, It''s easy on the eyes, and mind. I also did not vote on this challenge, but i would have rated it very high." I think this is a wonderful image, and i''m really disapointed it was rated so low.', '2004-11-24 17:34:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1031861, 121671, 17203, '<td valign="top">Ha, ha... me neither. The concept relies entirely on the distinctive background to stand out in the crowd. With more time, I might have been able to REALLY camouflage her or get a more interesting expression (she looks bored). This was like a 90 minute speed challenge for me, so I can''t complain.<br/> <br/>I still like it better than my October Free Study, though, and that one was one of my high scores, so I''ll be looking at it for a while. :-(</td>', 'Ha, ha... me neither. The concept relies entirely on the distinctive background to stand out in the crowd. With more time, I might have been able to REALLY camouflage her or get a more interesting expression (she looks bored). This was like a 90 minute speed challenge for me, so I can''t complain. I still like it better than my October Free Study, though, and that one was one of my high scores, so I''ll be looking at it for a while. :-(', '2004-11-24 17:45:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1031917, 121529, 29799, '<td valign="top">You know, what is makes a photo good? In my opinion, a photo is good if the mood and personality of the subjects comes through and evokes some emotion on those who view it. I think, if by looking at the photo you can get a feel for the subject''s personality, what an amazing capture that is! Learning about another person simply by looking at lines, curves, light and darkness. I see this photo as being a wonderful capture of their love for each other. By looking, I can see that these two are genuine and this adds to the overall wonderfuness of the photo. All the technicallity in the world means nothing if you can''t capture mood, and I believe that you have done that perfectly. High marks!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-24 19:01:59.</i></td>', 'You know, what is makes a photo good? In my opinion, a photo is good if the mood and personality of the subjects comes through and evokes some emotion on those who view it. I think, if by looking at the photo you can get a feel for the subject''s personality, what an amazing capture that is! Learning about another person simply by looking at lines, curves, light and darkness. I see this photo as being a wonderful capture of their love for each other. By looking, I can see that these two are genuine and this adds to the overall wonderfuness of the photo. All the technicallity in the world means nothing if you can''t capture mood, and I believe that you have done that perfectly. High marks!', '2004-11-24 18:55:41.000000', '2004-11-24 19:01:59.000000', 0),
(1031949, 121768, 1570, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> Well Done! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks, brad! this means a lot coming from a master like you!</td>', 'Originally posted by BradP: Well Done!   thanks, brad! this means a lot coming from a master like you!', '2004-11-24 19:37:41.000000', NULL, 0),
