(1034024, 122055, 6999, '<td valign="top">Not the kind of thing that appeals here - on dpc I mean - so that will have hurt your score more than anything. I like it though - the strict organisation of both the architecture and your POV and crop which suit it admirably. I don''t know if I would have used simply the blue channel - a single channel always tends to be very noisy. Don''t get me wrong, I''m a fan of some noise (viz. my own entries), but I think here it rather dominates too much. But it''s fun work, and I think a top photograph, certainly in potential, possibly let down just be that (for me) excessive noise. I can see that it helps the feel - but I think a more reserved use of it would not remove that element, and keep a tidier feel suiting the highly organised image.<br/> <br/>E</td>', 'Not the kind of thing that appeals here - on dpc I mean - so that will have hurt your score more than anything. I like it though - the strict organisation of both the architecture and your POV and crop which suit it admirably. I don''t know if I would have used simply the blue channel - a single channel always tends to be very noisy. Don''t get me wrong, I''m a fan of some noise (viz. my own entries), but I think here it rather dominates too much. But it''s fun work, and I think a top photograph, certainly in potential, possibly let down just be that (for me) excessive noise. I can see that it helps the feel - but I think a more reserved use of it would not remove that element, and keep a tidier feel suiting the highly organised image. E', '2004-11-27 04:53:11.000000', NULL, 0),
